    self.reserve(1);
    let start = self.as_mut_ptr();
    ptr = start.add(index);
    cur = ptr.add(num_added);
    ptr::copy(cur, cur.add(1), old_len - index);
    guard.start = start;
    ...
```

This matches upstream exactly, and upstream is considered fixed. Upstream's reserve is based on len, but whether set_len(0) causes a problem is subtle. Given the fixture annotation and the match with the fixed upstream, I judge it safe.

